    <h3 id="what-are-discount-collections">What are discount collections</h3>
    <p>Discount collections help you organize and manage multiple discount codes together. They're perfect for events, promotions, or when you need to create many similar discount codes at once.</p>
    <p>Collections allow you to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Group related discount codes together</li>
      <li>Set default discount parameters for all codes in a collection</li>
      <li>Bulk create multiple codes with similar settings</li>
      <li>Track usage and revenue across all codes in a collection</li>
      <li>Quickly create individual codes using collection defaults</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="create-collection">Create a discount collection</h3>
    <p>To create a discount collection, go to the <a href="https://gumroad.com/checkout/discount_collections">Discount Collections tab on the Checkout page</a>.</p>
    <p>Click "New collection" to get started. You'll need to provide:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Name:</strong> A descriptive name for your collection (e.g., "Summer Sale 2024", "Event Codes")</li>
      <li><strong>Description:</strong> Optional description to help you remember what the collection is for</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can also set default discount parameters that will be used when creating codes in this collection:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Discount Type:</strong> Percentage or fixed amount</li>
      <li><strong>Discount Value:</strong> The amount or percentage off</li>
      <li><strong>Max Uses:</strong> Maximum number of times each code can be used</li>
      <li><strong>Valid From/Until:</strong> When the codes become active and expire</li>
      <li><strong>Minimum Quantity:</strong> Minimum items required for the discount</li>
      <li><strong>Minimum Amount:</strong> Minimum purchase amount required</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="add-codes">Add discount codes to collections</h3>
    <p>Once you've created a collection, you can add discount codes to it in several ways:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>From the collection page:</strong> Click on a collection to view its details, then use "Bulk Create Codes" or "Quick Create Code"</li>
      <li><strong>From the discounts page:</strong> When creating or editing a discount code, you can assign it to a collection using the "Collection" dropdown</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Codes in a collection will inherit the collection's default settings, but you can override them for individual codes.</p>

    <h3 id="bulk-create">Bulk create codes</h3>
    <p>Bulk create allows you to generate multiple discount codes at once with similar settings:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to your collection and click "Bulk Create Codes"</li>
      <li>Set the number of codes you want to create</li>
      <li>Choose a name template (use {n} for automatic numbering, e.g., "Event Code {n}")</li>
      <li>Configure the discount settings (or use collection defaults)</li>
      <li>Select which products the codes apply to</li>
      <li>Set any additional restrictions (usage limits, validity period, etc.)</li>
      <li>Click "Create codes"</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Each code will be unique and can be used independently. This is perfect for events where you need many individual codes.</p>

    <h3 id="quick-create">Quick create codes</h3>
    <p>Quick create lets you generate individual codes using your collection's default settings:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to your collection and click "Quick Create Code"</li>
      <li>Enter a name for the code</li>
      <li>Click "Create"</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The new code will use all the default settings from your collection. This is great for creating codes on the fly during events or promotions.</p>
    <p><strong>Note:</strong> Quick create is only available if your collection has default discount parameters set.</p>

    <h3 id="edit-collections">Edit collections</h3>
    <p>To edit a collection:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to the Discount Collections page</li>
      <li>Click on the collection you want to edit</li>
      <li>Click "Edit" in the side panel</li>
      <li>Update the name, description, or default settings</li>
      <li>Click "Save changes"</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Changes to default settings will only affect new codes created in the collection. Existing codes won't be modified.</p>

    <h3 id="delete-collections">Delete collections</h3>
    <p>When deleting a collection, you have two options:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Keep the discount codes:</strong> The collection will be deleted, but all discount codes will remain active and functional</li>
      <li><strong>Delete the discount codes too:</strong> Both the collection and all its discount codes will be permanently deleted</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Choose carefully, as deleting codes will make them unusable for customers.</p>

    <h3 id="faqs">FAQs</h3>

    <p><strong>Q: Can I move discount codes between collections?</strong></p>
    <p>Yes! When editing a discount code, you can change which collection it belongs to using the "Collection" dropdown.</p>

    <p><strong>Q: Do I need to set default parameters for my collection?</strong></p>
    <p>No, default parameters are optional. You can create a collection just for organization and set individual parameters for each code.</p>

    <p><strong>Q: Can I use the same discount code in multiple collections?</strong></p>
    <p>No, each discount code can only belong to one collection at a time.</p>

    <p><strong>Q: How do I track which codes belong to which collection?</strong></p>
    <p>On the Discounts page, you can filter by collection using the "Collection" filter dropdown. You can also view all codes in a collection by clicking on the collection name.</p>

    <p><strong>Q: Can I export all codes from a collection?</strong></p>
    <p>Yes! Click on a collection to view its details, then click "Export CSV" to download all the codes in that collection.</p>

    <p><strong>Q: What happens if I delete a collection but keep the codes?</strong></p>
    <p>The codes will remain active and functional, but they won't be associated with any collection. You can reassign them to a different collection later.</p>

    <p><strong>Q: Can I use collections for affiliate codes?</strong></p>
    <p>Collections are designed for discount codes, not affiliate codes. Affiliate codes are managed separately in the Affiliates section.</p>
